# Fortuna Project - Current Context

## 1) Project objective
- Name: `fortuna`
- Purpose: personal financial management application.
- Current state: initial Node.js + TypeScript bootstrap.

## 2) Decisions already made
- Chosen license: Apache 2.0.
- Primary language: TypeScript.
- JavaScript module system: ESM (`"type": "module"`).
- Minimum Node.js version: `>=20.0.0`.
- Build output directory: `dist/`.
- npm distribution as a single bundle via `tsup` in `dist/fortuna.js` (minified, no sourcemap).
- Code quality stack: `ESLint` (modern flat config) + `Prettier`.

## 3) Licensing
- License file created: `LICENSE`.
- `package.json` updated with `"license": "Apache-2.0"`.
- Copyright:
  - `Copyright 2026 Fabiano Pires (Mineot)`.

## 4) Current file structure
- `package.json`: project metadata and scripts.
- `package-lock.json`: npm lockfile.
- `tsconfig.json`: TypeScript compiler config.
- `tsconfig.eslint.json`: dedicated ESLint config (type-aware lint including `tsup.config.ts`).
- `eslint.config.mjs`: modern lint configuration with Prettier integration.
- `.prettierrc`: formatting rules.
- `.prettierignore`: Prettier exclusions.
- `src/main.ts`: current entrypoint.
- `LICENSE`: Apache License 2.0 text.
- `.codex`: this project context.
- `.gitignore`: ignores `dist/` and `node_modules/`.
- Historical note: entrypoint was renamed from `src/index.ts` to `src/main.ts`.

## 5) Installed dev dependencies
- `typescript` (`^5.8.3`)
- `tsx` (`^4.19.3`)
- `@types/node` (`^22.15.3`)
- `tsup` (`^8.5.1`)
- `eslint` (`^9.x`)
- `@typescript-eslint/parser` (`^8.x`)
- `@typescript-eslint/eslint-plugin` (`^8.x`)
- `eslint-config-prettier` (`^10.x`)
- `prettier` (`^3.x`)
- `globals` (`^16.x`)

## 6) Configured npm scripts
- `build`: `tsup`
- `lint`: `eslint .`
- `lint:fix`: `eslint . --fix`
- `format`: `prettier . --write`
- `format:check`: `prettier . --check`
- `dev`: `tsx watch src/main.ts`
- `start`: `node dist/fortuna.js`
- `check`: `tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json`

## 7) TypeScript configuration (tsconfig)
- Modern ECMAScript target: `target: ESNext`
- Modern library set: `lib: ["ESNext"]`
- Node module format: `module: NodeNext`
- Module resolution: `moduleResolution: NodeNext`
- Strict mode enabled: `strict: true`
- Additional safety flags:
  - `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`
  - `exactOptionalPropertyTypes`
  - `isolatedModules`
  - `verbatimModuleSyntax`
- Artifact generation:
  - `declaration: true`
  - `declarationMap: true`
  - `sourceMap: true`
- Directories:
  - input: `src/`
  - output: `dist/`

## 8) Known notes
- npm distribution build:
- Entry: `src/main.ts`
- Single output file: `dist/fortuna.js`
- Minification: enabled
- Sourcemap: disabled
- Lint and format should run before npm publish.
- Type-aware ESLint uses `tsconfig.eslint.json` to avoid files outside `rootDir` from `tsconfig.json`.
- Current Prettier rules:
- `singleQuote: true`
- `trailingComma: "all"`
- `semi: true`
- `printWidth: 100`
- `tabWidth: 2`

## 9) Conventions for next changes
- Keep TypeScript sources in `src/` and build output in `dist/`.
- Prefer modern configuration (`ESNext`) unless compatibility requires otherwise.
- Mandatory rule: always update this file (`.codex`) whenever architecture, scripts, tooling, folder structure, or build/runtime flow changes.

## 10) Collaboration flow (terminal)
- Agreed flow:
- The user runs only installation commands when requested (`npm install`, `npm i`, `npm install -D`, etc.).
- The agent performs all other configuration and file changes directly in the project.
